§ `s 3 and Arts 1 to 6`

#ASSERT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `a Singapore importer buying lathes from a German maker`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `a Singapore importer buying from a maker in a non-Contracting State`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `a tourist buying a watch for herself from a shop abroad`
#ASSERT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `personal-use goods ordered on a company letterhead`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `two Singapore firms trading with each other`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `a foreign seller dealing through a Singapore office without disclosing it`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `a cross-border auction of machinery`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention governs the sale in Singapore` `goods made in Singapore from materials the foreign buyer supplies`

#ASSERT `the Convention would govern without the section 3(2) reservation` `a Singapore importer buying from a maker in a non-Contracting State`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention would govern without the section 3(2) reservation` `two Singapore firms trading with each other`

#ASSERT `the Convention answers the question` `whether a contract was formed`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention answers the question` `whether the contract is valid`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention answers the question` `the seller's liability for personal injury caused by the goods`

§ `Arts 14, 16, 19`

#ASSERT `the proposal is an offer` `a quotation to one buyer naming goods, quantity and price`
#ASSERT NOT `the proposal is an offer` `a price catalogue mailed to the trade`
#ASSERT NOT `the proposal is an offer` `an order to one seller with no price and no way to fix one`
#ASSERT `the proposal is an offer` `an advertisement stating it is a firm offer to the first comer`

#ASSERT `the revocation is effective` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the revocation is effective` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the revocation is effective` TRUE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `the reply is an acceptance` `no modification` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the reply is an acceptance` `an arbitration clause` FALSE
#ASSERT `the reply is an acceptance` `a non-material addition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the reply is an acceptance` `a non-material addition` TRUE

§ `Arts 25, 46, 49, 82`

#ASSERT `the breach is fundamental` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the breach is fundamental` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the breach is fundamental` TRUE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `the buyer may declare the contract avoided` `a buyer of goods with a fundamental defect who acts promptly`
#ASSERT `the buyer may declare the contract avoided` `a buyer still without the goods after the additional period`
#ASSERT NOT `the buyer may declare the contract avoided` `a buyer facing a minor defect`
#ASSERT NOT `the buyer may declare the contract avoided` `a buyer who waited too long`
#ASSERT `the buyer may declare the contract avoided` `a buyer who resold the goods before the defect could be found`
#ASSERT NOT `the buyer may declare the contract avoided` `a buyer whose seller is late with no additional period fixed`

#ASSERT `the buyer may require substitute goods` `a buyer of goods with a fundamental defect who acts promptly`
#ASSERT NOT `the buyer may require substitute goods` `a buyer still without the goods after the additional period`
#ASSERT NOT `the buyer may require substitute goods` `a buyer who damaged the goods himself`

